=== CloudVerb create path, clean and level ===
/cloud cannot start a new cloud session for dv5 rig. This engine drives claude 2.1.246, and starting one is interactive-only there:

Error: --cloud requires an interactive terminal.
Non-interactive invocations (piped stdout, --init-only, --sdk-url) run locally and would silently ignore --cloud. Drop --cloud, or run from a TTY.

Run this on a terminal, then send follow-ups from here with /cloud <session-id> <message>:

claude --cloud "sweep the docs"

dv5 rig is ready for it: main at bff6d5d1, clean, and origin/main has the same commit.

=== ClaudeCloudCli against the REAL claude binary (bogus session id) ===
argv: claude -p "say ok" --cloud 00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000
exit=1 timedOut=False
stdout: 
stderr: Error: --cloud "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000" is not a cloud session ID or URL.
With --print, --cloud sends the prompt to an existing cloud session: pass its ID (session_... or cse_...) or its claude.ai/code URL. To start a new cloud session from a description instead, drop --print.

